IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Apportionment Act 1928 (Singapore) -- whether a rent, salary, pension, dividend or other periodical payment is shared out
-- by the day when an interest in it ends part-way through a period (ss 2, 3, 6, 7), how much has accrued (s 3, s 5(1)
-- allowances), when the share can be recovered (s 4), and who can recover it, from whom and how (s 5).
--
-- SEAT: the person whose interest in a periodical payment ends part-way through a period -- the landlord, the pensioner, the
-- employee, the shareholder -- or that person's executor, administrator or assign (for a death, the heir's side of the
-- estate). Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 2 ("annuities", "dividends", "rents"), s 3, s 4(a) and (b), s 5(1) and (2), s 6, s 7.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December
-- 2021), SSO "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/AA1928.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title) and the long title, which decide nothing. The Act has no subsidiary instruments, numbers,
-- time limits or official discretions to bring in. What the general law gives for a payment the Act does NOT apportion
-- (ss 6, 7, a return of capital, a lump sum) is not encoded: those cases answer NOTHING, never zero.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Apportionment Act 1928`

§§ `2. Interpretation -- the kinds of payment`

-- s 2: "annuities" includes salaries and pensions.
-- s 2: "rents" includes "all periodical payments or renderings in lieu of or in the nature of rent".
-- s 2: "dividends" includes "all payments made by the name of dividend, bonus or otherwise out of the revenue of trading or
-- other public companies, divisible between all or any of the members", "but does not include payments in the nature of a
-- return or reimbursement of capital".
-- s 3: "All rents, annuities, dividends and other periodical payments in the nature of income".
DECLARE `Kind of payment` IS ONE OF
    `rent`                                                -- includes payments in lieu of or in the nature of rent (s 2)
    `an annuity, salary or pension`                       -- "annuities" includes salaries and pensions (s 2)
    `a dividend or bonus out of a company's revenue`      -- s 2 "dividends"
    `another periodical payment in the nature of income`  -- the residual words of s 3
    `a payment that is not periodical income`             -- a lump sum, a one-off fee: outside s 3

-- Who is asking. s 5(1): "All persons and their respective executors, administrators and assigns, and also the executors,
-- administrators and assigns respectively of persons whose interests determine with their own deaths".
DECLARE `Who I am` IS ONE OF
    `the person whose interest ended`
    `that person's executor or administrator`
    `that person's assign`
    `someone with no interest in the payment`

-- How the interest ended. s 4(a) "a continuing rent, annuity, or other such payment"; s 4(b) one "determined by re-entry,
-- death, or otherwise".
DECLARE `How it ended` IS ONE OF
    `the payment continues to someone else`               -- s 4(a): e.g. my life interest ends, the rent goes on to the next owner
    `the payment itself stopped by re-entry, death or otherwise` -- s 4(b)

-- The facts the person can state about one payment and the day their interest in it ended.
DECLARE `My payment` HAS
    `the kind`                                       IS A `Kind of payment`
    `it is a return or reimbursement of capital`     IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 2: such a payment is not a "dividend"
    `it is an annual sum under a policy of assurance` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 6
    `it is expressly stipulated that no apportionment shall take place` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 7
    `it is made payable under an instrument in writing` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 3: "under an instrument in writing or otherwise"
    `the entire portion`                             IS A NUMBER    -- the whole payment for the period, in dollars
    `the period began on`                            IS A DATE      -- the previous due date; for a dividend, the start of
                                                                    -- the period it is declared for (s 2)
    `the entire portion falls due on`                IS A DATE      -- for s 4(b): would have fallen due, had it not stopped
    `the period ends on`                             IS A DATE      -- the end of the period the entire portion is for
    `my interest ended on`                           IS A DATE
    `how it ended`                                   IS A `How it ended`
    `just allowances for the whole period`           IS A NUMBER    -- s 5(1): deductions properly charged on the entire portion
    `it is rent reserved out of or charged on land`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 5(2)

§§ `3. Rents, etc., to accrue from day to day -- with the exclusions in ss 2, 6 and 7`

-- s 3: "All rents, annuities, dividends and other periodical payments in the nature of income (whether reserved or made payable
-- under an instrument in writing or otherwise) shall, like interest on money lent, be considered as accruing from day to day,
-- and shall be apportionable in respect of time accordingly."
GIVEN p IS A `My payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is it periodical income within section 3` p IF
    CONSIDER p's `the kind`
    WHEN `rent`                                               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an annuity, salary or pension`                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a dividend or bonus out of a company's revenue`     THEN NOT p's `it is a return or reimbursement of capital`
    WHEN `another periodical payment in the nature of income` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a payment that is not periodical income`            THEN FALSE

-- s 6: "Nothing in this Act shall render apportionable any annual sums made payable in policies of assurance of any
-- description."
-- s 7: "This Act shall not extend to any case in which it is expressly stipulated that no apportionment shall take place."
-- Whether the payment is in writing is deliberately not read: s 3 applies "under an instrument in writing or otherwise".
GIVEN p IS A `My payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my payment apportionable` p IF
        "s 3" ... `is it periodical income within section 3` p
    ... "s 6" ... NOT p's `it is an annual sum under a policy of assurance`
    ... "s 7" ... NOT p's `it is expressly stipulated that no apportionment shall take place`

-- Why the Act does or does not share out my payment, in the Act's own terms.
DECLARE `What the Act does with my payment` IS ONE OF
    `it accrues from day to day under section 3`
    `not periodical income, so outside section 3`
    `a return or reimbursement of capital, which section 2 takes out of "dividends"`
    `excluded by section 6 as an annual sum under a policy of assurance`
    `excluded by section 7 by express stipulation`

GIVEN p IS A `My payment`
GIVETH A `What the Act does with my payment`
DECIDE `What does the Act do with my payment` p IS
    BRANCH
      IF p's `it is expressly stipulated that no apportionment shall take place`
        THEN `excluded by section 7 by express stipulation`
      IF p's `it is an annual sum under a policy of assurance`
        THEN `excluded by section 6 as an annual sum under a policy of assurance`
      IF p's `the kind` EQUALS `a payment that is not periodical income`
        THEN `not periodical income, so outside section 3`
      IF p's `the kind` EQUALS `a dividend or bonus out of a company's revenue` AND p's `it is a return or reimbursement of capital`
        THEN `a return or reimbursement of capital, which section 2 takes out of "dividends"`
      OTHERWISE `it accrues from day to day under section 3`

§§ `3 and 5(1) -- how much has accrued to me`

-- s 3: "considered as accruing from day to day". s 2 (dividends): "deemed to have accrued by equal daily increment during and
-- within the period for or in respect of which the payment of the same revenue is declared or expressed to be made".
--
-- Counting days. The Act does not say how. READING TAKEN (an inference, not in the text): like interest on money lent, the
-- payment accrues for each whole day from the start of the period to the day the interest ends; the first day is not
-- counted and the last is. On that reading the whole period adds up to exactly the entire portion. Leap years are counted
-- from the calendar, never as 365.
GIVEN p IS A `My payment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in the period` p MEANS Day (p's `the period ends on`) MINUS Day (p's `the period began on`)

GIVEN p IS A `My payment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days that had run when my interest ended` p MEANS Day (p's `my interest ended on`) MINUS Day (p's `the period began on`)

-- The share of time is only an apportionment when the interest ends inside the period. Ending on or before the period began,
-- or on or after it ended, is not a part-way case: NOT COVERED by this encoding (the Act says nothing to it).
GIVEN p IS A `My payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `did my interest end part-way through the period` p IF
        `the days that had run when my interest ended` p GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the days that had run when my interest ended` p LESS THAN `the days in the period` p

-- The apportioned part before allowances. NOTHING means the Act does not apportion this payment, or the interest did not end
-- part-way through a period: either way this encoding gives no figure, and the answer is not zero.
GIVEN p IS A `My payment`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What part of the payment had accrued to me` p MEANS
    IF `Is my payment apportionable` p AND `did my interest end part-way through the period` p
    THEN JUST (p's `the entire portion` TIMES `the days that had run when my interest ended` p DIVIDED BY `the days in the period` p)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 5(1): remedies for the apportioned parts "(allowing proportionate parts of all just allowances)". The allowances are
-- shared in the same proportion of time as the payment. That they are shared by days is an inference from "proportionate".
GIVEN p IS A `My payment`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What can I recover after just allowances` p MEANS
    IF `Is my payment apportionable` p AND `did my interest end part-way through the period` p
    THEN JUST (  (p's `the entire portion` MINUS p's `just allowances for the whole period`)
               TIMES `the days that had run when my interest ended` p
               DIVIDED BY `the days in the period` p)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `4. When the apportioned part is payable`

-- s 4: "The apportioned part ... shall be payable or recoverable -- (a) in the case of a continuing rent, annuity, or other such
-- payment, when the entire portion of which such apportioned part forms part becomes due and payable, and not before; and
-- (b) in the case of a rent, annuity, or other such payment determined by re-entry, death, or otherwise, when the next entire
-- portion of the same would have been payable if the same had not so determined, and not before."
DECLARE `Limb of section 4` IS ONE OF
    `section 4(a): when the entire portion becomes due`
    `section 4(b): when the next entire portion would have been payable`

GIVEN p IS A `My payment`
GIVETH A `Limb of section 4`
`Which limb of section 4 fixes when I am paid` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `how it ended`
    WHEN `the payment continues to someone else`                      THEN `section 4(a): when the entire portion becomes due`
    WHEN `the payment itself stopped by re-entry, death or otherwise` THEN `section 4(b): when the next entire portion would have been payable`

-- Both limbs land on the due date of the entire portion of which my share forms part: under (a) the day it actually falls
-- due, under (b) the day it would have fallen due. NOTHING where the Act does not apportion the payment (as above).
GIVEN p IS A `My payment`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`When can I recover my share` p MEANS
    IF `Is my payment apportionable` p AND `did my interest end part-way through the period` p
    THEN JUST (p's `the entire portion falls due on`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "and not before": on a given day, may I yet recover it?
GIVEN p IS A `My payment`, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I recover my share on` p `the day` IF
        `Is my payment apportionable` p
    AND `did my interest end part-way through the period` p
    AND Day `the day` AT LEAST Day (p's `the entire portion falls due on`)

§§ `5. Remedies -- who may recover, from whom, and how`

-- s 5(1): "All persons and their respective executors, administrators and assigns, and also the executors, administrators and
-- assigns respectively of persons whose interests determine with their own deaths, shall have such or the same remedies for
-- recovering such apportioned parts as aforesaid when payable ... as they respectively would have had for recovering the
-- entire portions as aforesaid if entitled thereto".
GIVEN `I am` IS A `Who I am`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have the remedies of section 5` `I am` IF
    CONSIDER `I am`
    WHEN `the person whose interest ended`         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `that person's executor or administrator` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `that person's assign`                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `someone with no interest in the payment` THEN FALSE

-- s 5(2): "Persons liable to pay rents reserved out of or charged on lands or tenements, and the same lands or tenements, shall
-- not be resorted to for any such apportioned part forming part of an entire or continuing rent as aforesaid specifically,
-- but the entire or continuing rent, including such apportioned part, shall be recovered and received by the person who, if
-- the rent had not been apportionable ... would have been entitled to the entire or continuing rent, and the apportioned part
-- shall be recoverable from such person by the executors or other parties entitled under this Act to the same by suit."
DECLARE `How I recover my share` IS ONE OF
    `from the payer, with the same remedies as for the entire portion`
    `by suit against whoever receives the entire rent, not from the tenant or the land`
    `the Act gives me no remedy`

GIVEN p IS A `My payment`, `I am` IS A `Who I am`
GIVETH A `How I recover my share`
`How do I recover my share` p `I am` MEANS
    IF     NOT `Do I have the remedies of section 5` `I am`
        OR NOT `Is my payment apportionable` p
        OR NOT `did my interest end part-way through the period` p
    THEN `the Act gives me no remedy`
    ELSE IF p's `it is rent reserved out of or charged on land`
         THEN `by suit against whoever receives the entire rent, not from the tenant or the land`
         ELSE `from the payer, with the same remedies as for the entire portion`

-- s 5(2), as the question asked: may I go straight to the payer (for rent on land, the tenant or the land) for my share?
GIVEN p IS A `My payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I go to the payer directly for my share` p IF
        `Is my payment apportionable` p
    AND `did my interest end part-way through the period` p
    AND NOT p's `it is rent reserved out of or charged on land`
